IMPORT prelude

-- Electricity Act 2001 (Singapore) -- what I may do myself with wiring and the ground, and what I can be charged with:
-- electrical work (s 82), digging near cables (ss 79, 80), the offences of Part 10 and their maxima, stealing
-- electricity and the meter-tampering presumption (s 87), my company's offences (s 91), composition (s 93), serious
-- accidents on my premises (s 94) and arrest (s 96).
--
-- SEAT: the individual occupier or owner of premises -- the householder who changes a fuse, hires an electrician, digs
-- in the garden or keeps the meter -- asked as the person who may be charged.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 2 ("high voltage", "low voltage", "electrical work", "earthworks"), s 79, s 80 (with the
-- s 80(9) and (10) defence), s 82(1), (5), (7) to (9), ss 72, 79(5), 80(7), (8), 83 to 89 and 92 (the maxima), s 87
-- (the fine formula and the presumption), s 91, s 93, s 94(1) to (7) and s 96.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1/9/2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EA2001.txt, with amendments to Act 27 of 2024 (in force 1 July 2025) shown.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: cable detection licensing (s 81), the duties of installation licensees beyond their offences (ss 72 to
-- 76), s 85's defence (shaped like s 80(9) and (10) but not separately encoded), s 89's elements, the conduct of the
-- accident inquiry (s 95), s 90 (jurisdiction), and the regulations prescribing compoundable offences
-- (s 93(2)), which are not deposited: whether my offence is prescribed is a fact I state.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual occupier, with the design
-- defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electricity Act 2001 -- what I may do, and what I can be charged with`

§§ `2 -- high voltage and low voltage`

-- s 2: "high voltage" means "a voltage exceeding 1000V a.c. or 1500V d.c. between conductors, or 600V a.c. or 900V d.c.
-- between each conductor and Earth"; "low voltage" means "a voltage not exceeding 1000V a.c. or 1500V d.c. between
-- conductors, or 600V a.c. or 900V d.c. between each conductor and Earth".
-- Read literally, a voltage that exceeds one limit but not the other meets BOTH definitions. This encoding treats it as
-- high voltage (an inference: the stricter regime of s 80 governs). See NOTES.md.
DECLARE `Current` IS ONE OF
    `alternating current`
    `direct current`

GIVEN `the current`                IS A `Current`
      `volts between conductors`   IS A NUMBER
      `volts to Earth`             IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the cable high voltage` IF
    CONSIDER `the current`
    WHEN `alternating current` THEN `volts between conductors` GREATER THAN 1000 OR `volts to Earth` GREATER THAN 600
    WHEN `direct current`      THEN `volts between conductors` GREATER THAN 1500 OR `volts to Earth` GREATER THAN 900

§§ `2 and 82 -- may I do this electrical work myself`

-- s 2: "electrical work" means "any work performed or carried out on any electrical installation" including installing,
-- repairing, altering, replacing or adding any part, "but does not include work in relation to -- (a) the
-- manufacturing of any electrical installation ...; or (b) the oiling, greasing, cleaning or painting of any electrical
-- installation". "electrical installation" excludes "(b) any appliance, wire, fitting or apparatus connected to and
-- beyond any electrical outlet ... at which fixed wiring terminates". Work on a plugged-in appliance is therefore not
-- "electrical work" at all (derived from the two definitions).
-- s 82(1): "An individual must not carry out, or offer or undertake to carry out, any electrical work unless -- (a) the
-- individual is a licensed electrical worker; or (b) the individual acts under the supervision of an individual who is a
-- licensed electrical worker." s 2: "licensed" -- holding a licence "permitting him or her to perform personally such
-- electrical work as is specified in his or her licence".
-- s 82(8): "it is not unlawful for -- (a) a person to replace any lamp that is connected in the person's own electrical
-- installation; (b) a person to replace any fuse in the person's own electrical installation similar to that of a
-- household; ... (e) a person, other than an electrical worker, whose trade or occupation normally includes the
-- performance of work on any appliance, plant or machinery ... so long as the person does not carry out work on any part
-- or circuit which is, or may be, connected to a source of electricity supply; and (f) a trained person to carry out any
-- work in accordance with the written instructions of the licensed electrical worker in charge". (9): a "trained
-- person" is an employee recognised by the employer and that worker as having the knowledge and experience to avoid
-- danger, and capable of the work. (c) and (d) save the Authority and its staff, never this seat.
-- s 82(7): contravention is an offence; no penalty is stated, so s 92 applies.
DECLARE `The job` IS ONE OF
    `replacing a lamp`
    `replacing a household-type fuse`
    `adding or altering wiring, sockets or switches`
    `repairing an appliance plugged into a socket`
    `cleaning or painting the installation`
    `repairing a machine in my non-electrical trade, off any circuit that is or may be connected to supply`
    `repairing a machine in my non-electrical trade, on a circuit that is or may be connected to supply`
    `following the written instructions of the licensed electrical worker in charge, as a trained employee`

DECLARE `My electrical job` HAS
    `the job`                                                      IS A `The job`
    `the installation is my own`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a licensed electrical worker and my licence covers it`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I act under the supervision of a licensed electrical worker`  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Electrical work answer` IS ONE OF
    `it is not electrical work under section 2`
    `yes: I am licensed for it`
    `yes: I am supervised by a licensed electrical worker`
    `yes: section 82(8) saves it`
    `no: it is an offence under section 82(7)`

GIVEN `the job` IS A `My electrical job`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it electrical work` IF
    CONSIDER `the job`'s `the job`
    WHEN `repairing an appliance plugged into a socket` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `cleaning or painting the installation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the job` IS A `My electrical job`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 82(8) save it` IF
    CONSIDER `the job`'s `the job`
    WHEN `replacing a lamp` THEN `the job`'s `the installation is my own`
    WHEN `replacing a household-type fuse` THEN `the job`'s `the installation is my own`
    WHEN `repairing a machine in my non-electrical trade, off any circuit that is or may be connected to supply` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `following the written instructions of the licensed electrical worker in charge, as a trained employee` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the job` IS A `My electrical job`
GIVETH A `Electrical work answer`
DECIDE `May I do this electrical work myself` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Is it electrical work` `the job`
              THEN `it is not electrical work under section 2`
           IF `the job`'s `I am a licensed electrical worker and my licence covers it`
              THEN `yes: I am licensed for it`
           IF `the job`'s `I act under the supervision of a licensed electrical worker`
              THEN `yes: I am supervised by a licensed electrical worker`
           IF `Does section 82(8) save it` `the job`
              THEN `yes: section 82(8) saves it`
           OTHERWISE `no: it is an offence under section 82(7)`

-- s 82(5): "An owner or occupier of any premises who wishes to have any electrical work carried out at the premises
-- must not knowingly engage (whether with or without consideration) a person that is not permitted under subsection (1)
-- or (3)". Only knowing engagement is caught.
GIVEN `the person I engaged is permitted under section 82(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I knew they were not permitted`                               IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by engaging this person for electrical work` IF
    (NOT `the person I engaged is permitted under section 82(1) or (3)`) AND `I knew they were not permitted`

§§ `2, 79 and 80 -- may I dig near an electricity cable`

-- s 2: "earthworks" means "(a) any act of excavating earth, rock or other material (by whatever means); (b) any act done
-- on, in or under the ground in connection with [building, road, pipe or cable work, or] (iii) any soil investigation
-- work ...; (c) any act of boring, dredging, jacking, levelling, piling or tunnelling on or under any premises or street
-- by any mechanical means; or (d) the driving or sinking of any bar, rod, pole, picket, casing or tube into the ground".
-- s 79(1): no earthworks "within the vicinity of any low voltage electricity cable which belongs to or which is under
-- the management or control of an electricity licensee unless the person has caused cable detection work to be carried
-- out by a licensed cable detection worker". (5): "$10,000 or ... 12 months or ... both".
-- s 80(1): near a HIGH voltage cable of a licensee, not unless the person "(a) has given to the electricity licensee not
-- less than 7 days' written notice ...; (b) has obtained from the electricity licensee the necessary information on the
-- location ... and has consulted the electricity licensee ...; and (c) has caused cable detection work to be carried
-- out by a licensed cable detection worker". (3): "The Authority may, if it thinks fit, modify the period" (so the
-- period is an input, 7 unless modified). (4): the further duties to comply with the licensee's reasonable requirements,
-- take reasonable precautions and allow access. (7): breach of (1) or (4) -- "$100,000 or ... 5 years or ... both".
-- (11): s 80 (except (1)(c)) also applies to infrastructure housing a transmission cable of 66 kilovolts or more.
-- s 79(2), s 80(6): neither prohibits earthworks where the person "has reasonable cause to believe that it is necessary
-- to do so in the interest of public or private safety except that the person must, not more than 7 days after the
-- earthworks have been commenced or carried out, give to the electricity licensee written notice stating the nature and
-- extent of those earthworks". s 79(3), s 80(6A) free the licensee that owns the cable, never this seat.
DECLARE `The kind of work` IS ONE OF
    `excavating earth, rock or other material`
    `boring, levelling, piling or tunnelling by mechanical means`
    `driving a bar, rod, pole, picket, casing or tube into the ground`
    `soil investigation work`
    `work above the ground only`

DECLARE `The cable nearby` IS ONE OF
    `no licensee's cable in the vicinity`
    `a licensee's low voltage cable`
    `a licensee's high voltage cable, or infrastructure housing a transmission cable`

DECLARE `My earthworks` HAS
    `the kind of work`                                                           IS A `The kind of work`
    `the cable nearby`                                                           IS A `The cable nearby`
    `I have reasonable cause to believe it is necessary for public or private safety` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of written notice I gave the licensee before starting`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the notice period in days, 7 unless the Authority modified it`              IS A NUMBER
    `I obtained the cable location from the licensee and consulted it`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a licensed cable detection worker carried out cable detection work`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I met the licensee's reasonable requirements, took precautions and allowed it access` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Earthworks answer` IS ONE OF
    `sections 79 and 80 do not apply`
    `allowed for safety: written notice to the licensee is due within 7 days of starting`
    `allowed: I took the steps the section requires`
    `an offence under section 79(5): up to $10,000 or 12 months or both`
    `an offence under section 80(7): up to $100,000 or 5 years or both`

GIVEN `the works` IS A `My earthworks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are they earthworks` IF
    NOT (`the works`'s `the kind of work` EQUALS `work above the ground only`)

GIVEN `the works` IS A `My earthworks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I take the section 80 steps` IF
        `the works`'s `days of written notice I gave the licensee before starting` AT LEAST `the works`'s `the notice period in days, 7 unless the Authority modified it`
    AND `the works`'s `I obtained the cable location from the licensee and consulted it`
    AND `the works`'s `a licensed cable detection worker carried out cable detection work`
    AND `the works`'s `I met the licensee's reasonable requirements, took precautions and allowed it access`

GIVEN `the works` IS A `My earthworks`
GIVETH A `Earthworks answer`
DECIDE `May I carry out these earthworks` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Are they earthworks` `the works`) OR `the works`'s `the cable nearby` EQUALS `no licensee's cable in the vicinity`
              THEN `sections 79 and 80 do not apply`
           IF `the works`'s `I have reasonable cause to believe it is necessary for public or private safety`
              THEN `allowed for safety: written notice to the licensee is due within 7 days of starting`
           IF `the works`'s `the cable nearby` EQUALS `a licensee's low voltage cable`
              THEN IF `the works`'s `a licensed cable detection worker carried out cable detection work`
                      THEN `allowed: I took the steps the section requires`
                      ELSE `an offence under section 79(5): up to $10,000 or 12 months or both`
           IF `Did I take the section 80 steps` `the works`
              THEN `allowed: I took the steps the section requires`
           OTHERWISE `an offence under section 80(7): up to $100,000 or 5 years or both`

-- The safety notice as a duty with its deadline. Whether a late notice is itself an offence is not said: s 79(5) and
-- s 80(7) punish contraventions of s 79(1) and s 80(1) and (4), and the notice duty sits in the exceptions. The breach
-- below therefore names no penalty.
DECLARE `Earthworks party` IS ONE OF
    `I, who carried out the earthworks`
    `the electricity licensee`

DECLARE `Earthworks action` IS ONE OF
    `give the licensee written notice stating the nature and extent of the earthworks`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Earthworks party` `Earthworks action`
`my duty to give notice after earthworks done for safety` MEANS
    PARTY `I, who carried out the earthworks`
    MUST  `give the licensee written notice stating the nature and extent of the earthworks`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `I, who carried out the earthworks`

-- s 80(9): "it is a defence for the person charged to prove -- (a) that the person took all reasonable steps to discharge
-- the person's duty under subsection (1) or (4) ...; or (b) that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised
-- all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence."
-- s 80(10) (Act 27 of 2024): if the defence "involves acting on information supplied by" the licensee, the owner of the
-- infrastructure, or "a licensed cable detection worker", the person "is not, without permission of the court, entitled
-- to rely on that defence unless, within 14 clear days before the hearing, the person charged has served on the
-- prosecutor a written notice" identifying the supplier.
-- "within 14 clear days before the hearing" is read as at least 14 clear days before it (an inference; see NOTES.md).
-- The court's permission is a judgment handed to someone else: an input.
GIVEN `I can prove reasonable steps, or reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my defence relies on information from the licensee, the infrastructure owner or a cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `clear days before the hearing that I served written notice on the prosecutor, 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
      `the court gives me permission`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I rely on the section 80(9) defence` IF
        `I can prove reasonable steps, or reasonable precautions and due diligence`
    AND (   NOT `my defence relies on information from the licensee, the infrastructure owner or a cable detection worker`
         OR `clear days before the hearing that I served written notice on the prosecutor, 0 if none` AT LEAST 14
         OR `the court gives me permission`)

§§ `72, 79 to 89 and 92 -- the most I can get for each offence`

-- Each row is read from the section named. "NOTHING" means the section provides no such punishment: s 6(2) has no
-- imprisonment, s 83(2) has no fine, and most sections state no daily fine. s 92: an offence "for which no penalty is
-- expressly provided" carries "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or
-- ... both and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... $250 for every day or part of a day". s 87's fine is a formula;
-- its row shows the fixed part (see below).
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 6(2) an unlicensed activity`
    `s 72(2) an installation not controlled by the directed electrical worker`
    `s 79(5) earthworks near a low voltage cable without cable detection`
    `s 80(7) earthworks near a high voltage cable in breach`
    `s 80(8) unlicensed cable detection near a high voltage cable`
    `s 82(7) unlicensed electrical work, or knowingly engaging an unlicensed person`
    `s 83(1) supplying electricity without an installation licence`
    `s 83(2) wilfully tampering with an installation so as to endanger life or property`
    `s 83(3) a rash or negligent act on my installation causing hurt or damage`
    `s 83(4) using an installation without an installation licence`
    `s 84 restoring a cut-off supply without the licensee's consent`
    `s 85(1) damaging the licensee's transmission plant or cable`
    `s 85A damaging a submarine cable`
    `s 86 pretending to be a licensee's employee to get in`
    `s 87 stealing electricity or tampering with the meter`
    `s 88 obstructing a licensee's employee, agent or contractor`
    `s 89 a false statement to the Authority`
    `s 94(7) failing to report a serious accident or altering the site`

DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `the most I can be fined, in dollars`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the longest I can be imprisoned, in months`                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the further fine for each day the offence continues after conviction` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
DECIDE `What is the most I can get for` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    --                                                                                        fine,         months,      per day
    WHEN `s 6(2) an unlicensed activity`                                     THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 500000, NOTHING,     JUST 12500
    WHEN `s 79(5) earthworks near a low voltage cable without cable detection` THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 10000,  JUST 12,     NOTHING
    WHEN `s 80(7) earthworks near a high voltage cable in breach`            THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 100000, JUST 60,     NOTHING
    WHEN `s 80(8) unlicensed cable detection near a high voltage cable`      THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 10000,  JUST 12,     NOTHING
    WHEN `s 83(1) supplying electricity without an installation licence`    THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 50000,  JUST 36,     NOTHING
    WHEN `s 83(2) wilfully tampering with an installation so as to endanger life or property` THEN `Maximum penalty` OF NOTHING, JUST 60, NOTHING
    WHEN `s 83(3) a rash or negligent act on my installation causing hurt or damage` THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 10000, JUST 36, NOTHING
    WHEN `s 83(4) using an installation without an installation licence`     THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 10000,  JUST 36,     JUST 250
    WHEN `s 84 restoring a cut-off supply without the licensee's consent`     THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 10000,  JUST 36,     JUST 250
    WHEN `s 85(1) damaging the licensee's transmission plant or cable`       THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 1000000, JUST 60,    NOTHING
    WHEN `s 85A damaging a submarine cable`                                  THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 2000000, JUST 60,    NOTHING
    WHEN `s 87 stealing electricity or tampering with the meter`             THEN `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 50000,  JUST 36,     JUST 250
    -- s 72(2) states the s 92 figures in terms; ss 82(7), 86, 88, 89 and 94(7) state none, so s 92 applies.
    OTHERWISE                                                                     `Maximum penalty` OF JUST 10000,  JUST 12,     JUST 250

§§ `87 -- stealing electricity and tampering with the meter`

-- s 87(1): an offence to "(a) dishonestly or fraudulently abstract[], use[], consume[] or divert[] any electricity
-- supplied by an electricity licensee; (b) alter[] or tamper[] with any part of any meter or meter installation ...;
-- (c) [compromise] the ability or proper operation of any meter ...; or (d) cause[] or permit[] any other person" to do so.
-- s 87(2): "(a) a fine that is the total of -- (i) an amount not exceeding $50,000; and (ii) an amount equal to 3 times
-- the value of electricity" abstracted or supplied; "(b) imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years", and $250 a day
-- for a continuing offence. (3): the value may be "fairly and reasonably estimated after comparing records ... of
-- electricity usage before, during and after".
-- Limb (ii) is "an amount equal to", not "not exceeding": the maximum grows with the value, with no ceiling.
GIVEN `the value of the electricity, in dollars`                        IS A NUMBER
      `days or part days the offence continues after conviction`       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for stealing electricity` MEANS
    50000 PLUS 3 TIMES `the value of the electricity, in dollars` PLUS 250 TIMES `days or part days the offence continues after conviction`

-- s 87(4) (as amended by Act 27 of 2024): on a charge of tampering, if it is proved "(a) that, at the time of the
-- alleged conduct -- (i) a device or wire was attached to, or was in the vicinity of, the meter ... for the purpose of
-- altering the index ... or preventing [it] from duly registering ...; (ii) the covering of the meter ... had a hole which
-- is not a result of ordinary wear and tear; (iii) any seal fastened by an electricity licensee ... was damaged, removed
-- or changed; (iv) any paint or other chemical compound applied by an electricity licensee ... was damaged or removed or
-- altered ...; or (v) the position or arrangement of any test link ... was changed or altered; and (b) that the person
-- had, at the time of the alleged conduct, custody or control of the meter", the person "is presumed, until the contrary
-- is proved", to have tampered.
DECLARE `My meter` HAS
    `a device or wire was attached to or near it to alter or stop its registering` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its covering had a hole that is not ordinary wear and tear`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `a licensee's seal on it was damaged, removed or changed`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a licensee's paint or compound on a screw or part was damaged, removed or altered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a test link on its terminal test block was moved`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had custody or control of it at the time`                                IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the meter` IS A `My meter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to have tampered with my meter` IF
        (   `the meter`'s `a device or wire was attached to or near it to alter or stop its registering`
         OR `the meter`'s `its covering had a hole that is not ordinary wear and tear`
         OR `the meter`'s `a licensee's seal on it was damaged, removed or changed`
         OR `the meter`'s `a licensee's paint or compound on a screw or part was damaged, removed or altered`
         OR `the meter`'s `a test link on its terminal test block was moved`)
    AND `the meter`'s `I had custody or control of it at the time`

§§ `91 and 93 -- my company's offences, and composition`

-- s 91: where a body of persons commits an offence, a person who "was a director, manager, secretary or other similar
-- officer or a partner ... or was purporting to act in any such capacity, shall be guilty of that offence ... unless the
-- person proves that -- (a) the offence was committed without the person's consent or connivance; and (b) the person
-- had exercised all such due diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as the person ought to have exercised".
GIVEN `I was, or purported to act as, a director, manager, secretary, similar officer or partner at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can prove it was done without my consent or connivance`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can prove I exercised all due diligence to prevent it`                  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of my company's offence` IF
        `I was, or purported to act as, a director, manager, secretary, similar officer or partner at the time`
    AND NOT (`I can prove it was done without my consent or connivance` AND `I can prove I exercised all due diligence to prevent it`)

-- s 93(1): "The Authority may, in its discretion, compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not
-- exceeding $3,000." The regulations prescribing the offences (s 93(2)) are not deposited, and the Authority's
-- discretion is its own: the answer is "only if the Authority chooses to".
GIVEN `my offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum asked of me, in dollars`          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my offence be compounded for this sum, if the Authority so chooses` IF
    `my offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum asked of me, in dollars` AT MOST 3000

§§ `94 -- a serious accident on my premises`

-- s 94(1): when an accident "causing or resulting in loss of life or hurt to any person or serious damage to property
-- has occurred in connection with any electrical or supply installation, or any other installation, the owner of the
-- premises concerned and the person granted a licence under Part 9 for the installation must -- (a) report the accident
-- to the Authority by the quickest means available; and (b) subsequently with the least possible delay, report in
-- writing". (7): contravening (1) or (3) "without lawful excuse" is an offence (s 92 penalty).
GIVEN `I own the premises or hold the Part 9 licence for the installation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone died`                                IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone was hurt`                            IS A BOOLEAN
      `property was seriously damaged`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report the accident to the Authority` IF
    `I own the premises or hold the Part 9 licence for the installation`
        AND (`someone died` OR `someone was hurt` OR `property was seriously damaged`)

-- s 94(3): "In the event of loss of life or grievous hurt ..., no alteration or addition may, without the approval of
-- the Authority, be made to any part of the installation which may have contributed towards the cause of the accident
-- or to the site of the accident until investigations have been completed." (4): "Nothing in subsection (3) operates to
-- interfere with rescue work or other work necessary for the general safety of life or property."
-- "grievous hurt" is borrowed from the Penal Code 1871: asked as a fact.
GIVEN `someone died or suffered grievous hurt`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigations have been completed`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved the change`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is rescue work or work needed for the safety of life or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I alter the installation or the accident site` IF
        NOT `someone died or suffered grievous hurt`
    OR  `the investigations have been completed`
    OR  `the Authority approved the change`
    OR  `the change is rescue work or work needed for the safety of life or property`

-- s 94(2): the authorised officer must visit, investigate and report, and "(e) if there has been any loss of life or
-- there is reason to believe that any person has been seriously injured, send a copy of his or her findings to the
-- Public Prosecutor". (5): the Authority "must hold an inquiry into the nature and cause of the accident" if "(a) it
-- appears to the Authority that there is reason to believe that the accident was due to any failure to comply with the
-- provisions of this Act or due to neglect to obey any lawful order given by the Authority; or (b) the authorised officer
-- investigating the accident is satisfied that the accident might have been prevented if proper precautions had been
-- taken". (6): the inquiry's findings and the Authority's opinion "must be forwarded to the Public Prosecutor".
-- These duties fall on officials; for me they say what will follow my report. Each official's belief or satisfaction is
-- a judgment handed to someone else: an input.
DECLARE `What follows my report` IS ONE OF
    `the officer's findings go to the Public Prosecutor, and an inquiry follows whose findings go there too`
    `an inquiry must be held, and its findings go to the Public Prosecutor`
    `the officer's findings go to the Public Prosecutor; no inquiry is required`
    `an investigation and report to the Authority only`

GIVEN `someone died, or there is reason to believe someone was seriously injured`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has reason to believe the accident was due to a failure to comply with the Act or its orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigating officer is satisfied proper precautions might have prevented it`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What follows my report`
DECIDE `What will follow my report of the accident` IS
    BRANCH IF     `someone died, or there is reason to believe someone was seriously injured`
              AND (   `the Authority has reason to believe the accident was due to a failure to comply with the Act or its orders`
                   OR `the investigating officer is satisfied proper precautions might have prevented it`)
              THEN `the officer's findings go to the Public Prosecutor, and an inquiry follows whose findings go there too`
           IF     `the Authority has reason to believe the accident was due to a failure to comply with the Act or its orders`
               OR `the investigating officer is satisfied proper precautions might have prevented it`
              THEN `an inquiry must be held, and its findings go to the Public Prosecutor`
           IF `someone died, or there is reason to believe someone was seriously injured`
              THEN `the officer's findings go to the Public Prosecutor; no inquiry is required`
           OTHERWISE `an investigation and report to the Authority only`

§§ `96 -- can I be arrested`

-- s 96(1): a police officer or a person authorised in writing by the Authority's Chief Executive "may arrest any person
-- committing within his or her view or who he or she has reason to believe has committed any offence punishable under
-- this Act if -- (a) the name and address of the person are unknown to him or her; (b) the person declines to give the
-- person's name and address; or (c) there is reason to doubt the accuracy of the name and address given." (2), (3): I
-- may be held until my name and address are ascertained, and no longer than needed to bring me before a court without
-- a court order. The officer's "reason to believe" is a judgment handed to someone else: an input.
GIVEN `the officer saw me commit an offence under the Act, or has reason to believe I did` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my name and address are unknown to the officer`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I decline to give my name and address`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is reason to doubt the name and address I gave`               IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be arrested under section 96` IF
    `the officer saw me commit an offence under the Act, or has reason to believe I did`
        AND (   `my name and address are unknown to the officer`
             OR `I decline to give my name and address`
             OR `there is reason to doubt the name and address I gave`)
